// Coding suite — did the END STATE match? Spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-23-eval-harness.md
//
// Every case here is SANDBOXED: `files` seeds a fresh tmpdir which becomes the
// case's project root, the turn runs in `build` mode, and `verify` runs in that
// tmpdir afterwards. Its exit code is the score. Nothing subjective enters it.
//
// FIXTURES ARE DEPENDENCY-FREE BY RULE (spec §4): plain `.mjs` and `node:assert`,
// run by `node`. The sandbox has no `node_modules`, no install step and no
// network, so `npx tsx` would need a package install per case — at exactly the
// point the harness is supposed to be boring. Cases that genuinely need the
// repo's toolchain are the Tier 2 sandbox (§6.2), which is not built.
//
// Every file `verify` names must appear in `files`, checker included; `dataset.ts`
// rejects the case at load otherwise, because a checker that was never created
// fails for the wrong reason and reads as an agent failure.
//
// `immutable` lists the checker. Saying "do not modify check.mjs" in the prompt
// is a request; this is the guard. An agent that edits the checker until it
// passes produces a green run that fixed nothing.
{"id": "fix-off-by-one", "prompt": "add() in calc.mjs returns the wrong result. Fix it. Do not modify check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "code-edit", "whyModelBacked": "Finding and fixing a bug from a one-line description is the whole task; there is no deterministic function that locates it.", "files": {"calc.mjs": "export const add = (a, b) => a - b;\n", "check.mjs": "import { add } from './calc.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.equal(add(2, 3), 5);\nassert.equal(add(-1, 1), 0);\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 10}
{"id": "implement-missing-export", "prompt": "check.mjs imports slugify from strings.mjs, but strings.mjs doesn't export it. Implement it so the checks pass. Do not modify check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "code-edit", "whyModelBacked": "Writing a function that satisfies an existing consumer requires reading the consumer and inferring the contract — inference, not lookup.", "files": {"strings.mjs": "export const trim = (s) => s.trim();\n", "check.mjs": "import { slugify } from './strings.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.equal(slugify('Hello World'), 'hello-world');\nassert.equal(slugify('  A  B  '), 'a-b');\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 10}
{"id": "fix-null-guard", "prompt": "lastItem() in list.mjs throws on an empty array. It should return undefined instead. Fix it without modifying check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "code-edit", "whyModelBacked": "Choosing the minimal guard rather than a rewrite is a judgement about scope that no deterministic checker makes.", "files": {"list.mjs": "export function lastItem(items) {\n  return items[items.length - 1].value;\n}\n", "check.mjs": "import { lastItem } from './list.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.equal(lastItem([]), undefined);\nassert.equal(lastItem([{ value: 1 }, { value: 2 }]), 2);\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 10}
{"id": "create-a-new-module", "prompt": "Create clamp.mjs exporting a clamp(n, min, max) function, so that check.mjs passes. Do not modify check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "code-edit", "whyModelBacked": "Creating a module from a checker's expectations means inferring an unstated signature.", "files": {"check.mjs": "import { clamp } from './clamp.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.equal(clamp(5, 0, 10), 5);\nassert.equal(clamp(-3, 0, 10), 0);\nassert.equal(clamp(42, 0, 10), 10);\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 10}
{"id": "fix-loop-bound", "prompt": "sum() in totals.mjs misses the last element. Fix the bug. Do not modify check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "code-edit", "whyModelBacked": "Off-by-one localisation from a symptom is exactly the inference under test.", "files": {"totals.mjs": "export function sum(nums) {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length - 1; i++) total += nums[i];\n  return total;\n}\n", "check.mjs": "import { sum } from './totals.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.equal(sum([1, 2, 3]), 6);\nassert.equal(sum([]), 0);\nassert.equal(sum([7]), 7);\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 10}
{"id": "fix-in-nested-dir", "prompt": "The parsePort function in src/config.mjs returns a string, but it should return a number. Fix it. Do not modify check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "code-edit", "whyModelBacked": "The file is named but the fix is not; picking a correct coercion is model work.", "files": {"src/config.mjs": "export function parsePort(raw) {\n  return raw ?? '8080';\n}\n", "check.mjs": "import { parsePort } from './src/config.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.strictEqual(parsePort('3000'), 3000);\nassert.strictEqual(parsePort(undefined), 8080);\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 10}
{"id": "recover-from-a-failing-command", "prompt": "Run `node run.mjs`. It fails. Read the error, work out what is missing, and make it run cleanly so that `node check.mjs` passes. Do not modify run.mjs or check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "recovery", "whyModelBacked": "The recovery only happens if the agent runs the command, reads a real stderr it has never seen, and infers the fix from it. A unit test can assert what run.mjs does; it cannot assert that an agent reacts to the failure instead of repeating it.", "files": {"run.mjs": "import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nconst raw = readFileSync('./settings.json', 'utf-8');\nconsole.log(JSON.parse(raw).name);\n", "check.mjs": "import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nconst out = execFileSync('node', ['run.mjs'], { encoding: 'utf-8' });\nassert.equal(out.trim(), 'freecode');\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["run.mjs", "check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 12}
{"id": "recover-from-a-wrong-path-in-the-prompt", "prompt": "There is a bug in src/format.mjs: pad() pads on the wrong side. Fix it so `node check.mjs` passes. Do not modify check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "recovery", "whyModelBacked": "The path in the prompt is wrong, so the first read fails. Whether the agent then searches for the real file or reports the prompt back as unanswerable is a judgement it makes from the error text.", "files": {"lib/format.mjs": "export const pad = (s, n) => s.padStart(n, '0');\n", "check.mjs": "import { pad } from './lib/format.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.equal(pad('7', 3), '007');\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 12}
{"id": "second-edit-must-see-the-first", "prompt": "In config.mjs, first rename the exported constant `timeout` to `timeoutMs`. Then, as a separate second edit, change its value to 5000. Both changes must be present in the final file. Do not modify check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "stale-context", "whyModelBacked": "The failure mode is the agent computing its second edit from the content it read BEFORE the first, which silently reverts the rename. Only a real turn with two sequential edits can produce it.", "files": {"config.mjs": "export const timeout = 5000;\n", "check.mjs": "import * as cfg from './config.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.equal(cfg.timeoutMs, 5000);\nassert.equal(cfg.timeout, undefined);\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 12}
{"id": "needle-in-a-huge-command-output", "prompt": "`node dump.mjs` prints over a million characters. Exactly one line starts with MARKER. Find the number on that line and write it to answer.mjs as `export const VALUE = <number>;`. Do not modify dump.mjs or check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "large-output", "whyModelBacked": "The bash tool keeps only the last 500KB, and MARKER is in the discarded head — so the answer is unreachable unless the agent filters at the shell instead of dumping and reading. Choosing to pipe is a model decision, not a code path.", "files": {"dump.mjs": "console.log('MARKER 8731');\nfor (let i = 0; i < 30000; i++) console.log(`row ${i} ${'x'.repeat(40)}`);\n", "check.mjs": "import { VALUE } from './answer.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.equal(VALUE, 8731);\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["dump.mjs", "check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 12}
{"id": "count-in-a-huge-command-output", "prompt": "`node dump.mjs` prints 30000 lines. Count exactly how many of them contain ERR, and write the count to answer.mjs as `export const COUNT = <number>;`. Do not modify dump.mjs or check.mjs.", "failureCategory": "large-output", "whyModelBacked": "An exact count over 30000 lines cannot be eyeballed from a truncated tool result; the agent has to delegate the counting to the shell. Whether it does that or guesses is the behaviour under test.", "files": {"dump.mjs": "for (let i = 0; i < 30000; i++) console.log(i % 219 === 0 ? `line ${i} ERR` : `line ${i} ok`);\n", "check.mjs": "import { COUNT } from './answer.mjs';\nimport assert from 'node:assert';\nassert.equal(COUNT, 137);\nconsole.log('ok');\n"}, "verify": "node check.mjs", "immutable": ["dump.mjs", "check.mjs"], "expectMaxTurns": 12}
